        "The most frequently reported issue with Evok modular furniture is connector and fitting failure. Evok's modular units use a combination of cam lock fittings, Rafix connectors, and wood dowels to assemble panels and modules. When these connectors loosen or strip -- particularly in particle board substrates -- the unit develops wobble, gaps between panels, and in severe cases, structural instability. Our modular furniture repair specialists carry compatible replacement hardware including cam locks, Rafix connectors, confirmat screws, and cross-dowels for Evok unit types. We repair stripped connector holes using wood filler and hardener or insert metal threaded inserts for a permanent fix.",
        "Wooden surface damage -- chipping, scratching, and finish wear -- is the second most common Evok furniture issue. The melamine or PU laminate surfaces used on Evok's engineered wood panels are durable for day-to-day use but chip at edges and corners when impacted. Scratches from keys, pet claws, or moving objects leave visible white or raw-wood marks in the laminate. Our <a href=\"/furniture-refinishing-delhi\">furniture refinishing service</a> uses colour-matched repair compounds and laminate repair kits to fill and colour-match chips and scratches to the surrounding surface, making damage nearly invisible. For extensively damaged panels, we can replace the surface laminate entirely.",
        "Sofa upholstery wear is the primary issue with Evok's seating range. Their sofas and sofa-beds use fabric or leatherette upholstery over foam cushions. The upholstery develops wear at armrests, seat fronts, and headrests over 3 to 5 years of regular use. Foam sagging is particularly common in Evok sofa-beds where the sofa-to-bed conversion mechanism puts additional stress on cushion foam. Our <a href=\"/sofa-repair-delhi\">sofa repair services</a> and <a href=\"/sofa-foam-replacement-delhi\">foam replacement service</a> address both these issues comprehensively.",
