        "Modular furniture repair is a specialist skill that sets FurniRevive apart from general furniture repair services. Evok's modular shelving units, wardrobes, TV units, and storage systems are assembled from standardised panels using precision hardware. When this hardware fails -- due to wear, overtightening, or movement -- the repair needs to be carried out with matching replacement hardware and proper knowledge of modular assembly systems. Using the wrong screw type or filling method can permanently damage particle board panels.",
        "Our modular repair process begins with a systematic check of all connector points in the affected unit. We identify every loose, stripped, or broken fitting. Where cam lock barrels have stripped in particle board, we use two-part epoxy wood filler to rebuild the substrate before inserting a new cam lock. For dowel holes that have widened, we fit replacement dowels of the next size up. For bracket fittings that have broken, we source replacement hardware from our stock of universal modular fittings. After all connectors are replaced and the unit is reassembled, we check all joints with a torque check to ensure consistent tension across the structure.",
        "We also repair Evok modular wardrobes -- a common request for customers in Rohini, Punjabi Bagh, and Paschim Vihar where Evok stores have a strong customer base. Wardrobe hinge failures, sagging wardrobe doors, stuck drawer runners, and loose shelf pin holes are all handled under our modular repair service. Pricing for modular connector repair starts from Rs.500 per fitting and Rs.2000 for a full connector audit and tighten on a modular unit. Wardrobe door hinge replacement starts from Rs.800 per door.",
